# Operating and maintenance manual for the crane installation cross

## Operating instructions

The normal operating temperature range for the installation cross is ${ \mathrm { o n } } + 0 ^ { \circ } { \mathrm { C } } \ldots + 5 0 ^ { \circ } { \mathrm { C } }$ . The installation cross must be stored protected from impacts and corrosive substances, preferably in a designated storage area. A copy of this manual and the dimensional/operating drawing must also be kept in the same location. 

Always before use, it must be visually inspected that the installation cross is in working condition and correctly attached. 

The installation cross may only be used for the purpose for which it was designed. Parts of the installation cross other than the lifting points intended for lifting must not be used for lifting. When ready for use, the installation cross must be leveled horizontally. 

When lifting the parts of the installation cross into place, no persons are allowed in the danger zone of a falling load. 

The lifting points of the various parts of the installation cross may only be used to lift that specific part, not to lift connected assemblies. An exception is the extended main and side beams, which can be lifted from their own respective lifting points. 

Under no circumstances should an attempt be made to lift the cross when it is loaded with counterweights ("ballast stones"). 

An extended beam here refers to either the main beam S171-1017, which has extension pieces S171-1025 bolted to both ends, or the side beam S171-1050, which has one extension piece S171-1025 bolted to it. 

A safety harness must be used whenever climbing onto the beams, working platforms, or access ladders. 

The main beam can be lifted by simultaneously using all four lifting points on the sides of the beam. 

